TASK (exactly one change):
The operator decided that the cli-opencode default model is `llmgateway/deepseek-v4.1-flash` on BOTH OpenCode versions. OpenCode 1 used `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash`, but the opencode-go quota is spent, and OpenCode 2 lists no opencode-go provider. One default now serves both.

In `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs`:
- Set `OPENCODE_DEFAULT_MODEL = 'llmgateway/deepseek-v4.1-flash'`.
- Delete the constant `OPENCODE_V2_DEFAULT_MODEL` and its entry in the module.exports list.
- In `buildOpencodeLineageCommand`, make the fallback `lineage.model || OPENCODE_DEFAULT_MODEL` with no version split.
- Rewrite the comment block above the defaults that explains the split ("The OpenCode fallback splits by major ...") so it says why one fallback serves both: OpenCode 2 lists no opencode-go provider, and llmgateway serves the same model on both majors. Keep it to two or three lines.
Do NOT touch any other opencode-go literal in the file (the route tables and the flash-max pin list stay; opencode-go remains a supported provider).

Tests:
1. `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/opencode-dual-dispatch.vitest.ts`: the test 'applies the OpenCode 1 default model to an unpinned lineage' must now expect `llmgateway/deepseek-v4.1-flash` (still with `--model`, `--variant`, `max`), and add one assertion that the argv does not contain `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash`. Leave the OpenCode 2 test as is.
2. `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/fanout-run.vitest.ts`: in the 'unpinned lineage fallbacks match their packets' table, delete the `OPENCODE_V2_DEFAULT_MODEL` row.

